From b4e84e04ce0fc992805f14ca2d09c043777fe598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban overlap same-creator guard: a denial is not a
 duplicate; an added round/sha is not an enumeration

Follow-ups from independent exact-head review 5893203646 of PR #2329 (card t_01a1d56ea127e910).

1. hermes_cli/kanban_dup_detector.py: `_DUP` matched denials ("Not a duplicate of t_X",
   "No duplicates found; parent t_X"), so a completion that says it is NOT a duplicate could open or
   comment the same-creator-duplicate detector card. `sibling_named` now scans each duplicate/supersede
   keyword and skips it when a negation (not/no/never/non-/...n't) sits up to two words before it in the
   same clause. A negation in an earlier clause ("No code changes; duplicate of t_X") still counts, and a
   denied keyword no longer swallows a later "superseded by t_Y".

2. hermes_cli/kanban_overlap_own.py: any digit-bearing token anywhere counted as an enumeration marker,
   so a re-issue whose title only adds "(round 2)" or a sha was admitted as fan-out whenever both titles
   carried any number (e.g. "PR #2329"). `enumerated()` now aligns the two titles' tokens
   (difflib opcodes) and counts markers only in a replaced span with a marker on both sides
   (w1-01/w1-02, worker-2/worker-3, 1/3 vs 3/3, fixture A/B, head sha vs head sha). An inserted marker is
   a re-issue and goes through the normal refusal.

Tests (RED on 8b0b242940d, GREEN here):
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py: 4 denial phrasings open nothing; earlier-clause negation
  and a later supersede still detected (5 failed before).
- tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py + fixture: two `reissue` replay cases (round 2,
  appended sha) are refused; added-number vs same-place-index unit cases (5 failed before). All 14
  recorded legitimate fan-outs and the 3 recorded duplicates are unchanged; the 3-completion detector
  replay still opens exactly one card.
- All 15 test files importing kanban_overlap / kanban_dup_detector / create_overlap: 435 passed, 1 skipped.
